    "commit_message_instructions": "<commit-format><subject>Start with present-tense verb (Add, Fix, Update, Refactor, Remove). Capitalize first letter. No trailing period. Under 50 chars. NO conventional commit prefixes (feat:, fix:, chore:, docs:, etc).</subject><body>Concise high-information summary, skip if change is simple. Explain why not how. Terse. Blank line after subject. Wrap at 72 chars. Skip if simple and Title is sufficient.</body><footer>Reference GitHub/Linear issues after body. Use Fixes #N to resolve, Refs #N to relate.</footer><examples><good>Add user authentication endpoint\\n\\nImplement /login route with email and password validation.\\nIntroduces bcrypt package for secure password hashing.\\n\\nFixes #123</good><bad>feat: add new login feature</bad><bad>fixed a bug</bad><bad>WIP</bad></examples></commit-format>",
    "commit_message_model": {
      "provider": "google",
      "model": "gemini-3.8-flash-low",
      "enable_thinking": false,
      "effort": "none"
    },
